    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0726" n="706" xml:id="pg706"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">792.5 MSP/1–2254:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 414<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in
                    Thailand</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-02-19T15:59:00-05:00">February 19, 1954—3:59
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1646. Your 1524.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d414-f1"/> Saraburi-Ban Phai Highway
                    discussed top level OCB meeting Feb 17 by
                    agencies concerned. Agreed jointly (1) approve for planning purposes principle
                    of highway construction; (2) stronger reasons especially military required to
                    justify high enough priority to secure funds for financing; (3) imperative that
                    Thai Govt also ardently desire highway and accordingly make formal request
                    through usual channels.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d414-f1" n="1" xml:id="d414-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 1524, Jan. 22, conveyed information regarding the estimated costs and
                    procedures involved in the proposed Saraburi-Ban Phai highway. (792.5 MSP/1–2254)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
